    "content": "Mogadishu, September 21, 2026 — Somalia's Upper House of Parliament approved the National Revenue Authority Establishment Bill on Monday, according to a report by Goobjoog. The legislation had previously cleared the Lower House, completing the parliamentary process. The bill now awaits implementation, which would create a national body responsible for managing and developing domestic revenue.\n\nThe proposed National Revenue Authority is expected to oversee the collection, administration, and growth of internal revenue streams. Its mandate includes reinforcing the tax system and other revenue sources, a key objective for a government seeking to reduce reliance on external aid. The bill's passage marks a step in a longer effort to formalize revenue institutions, though the authority is not yet operational.\n\nThe move comes amid broader discussions about Somalia's fiscal self-sufficiency. International partners have consistently urged the federal government to expand its domestic revenue base to fund public services and reduce dependency on foreign assistance. The establishment of a dedicated revenue authority is seen as a structural reform that could improve transparency and efficiency in tax collection.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, which sends substantial remittances and invests in businesses in Somalia, the new authority could affect the business environment. A more robust domestic revenue system may lead to clearer tax rules, potentially easing formal investment. However, it also raises questions about how taxation will be applied, especially for diaspora-owned enterprises that operate across multiple jurisdictions.\n\nThe bill's approval follows parliamentary procedures in both houses, but no timeline has been announced for the authority's launch. Implementation will require funding, staffing, and coordination with existing tax bodies. Observers note that similar reform efforts have faced capacity challenges in the past, and the authority's effectiveness will depend on political commitment and technical support.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/09/21/aqalka-sare-oo-ansixiyay-hindise-sharciyeedka-dhismaha-hayadda-dakhliga-qaranka/",
